WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.302
Constraints turn important business rules into rules
the database can enforce NOT

00:00:06.329 --> 00:00:11.016
NULL says a value is required DEFAULT supplies a
value when one

00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:17.345
is omitted UNIQUE protects candidate keys or other
non-duplicate rules CHECK

00:00:17.358 --> 00:00:23.779
evaluates a Boolean condition PRIMARY KEY defines
row identity FOREIGN

00:00:23.792 --> 00:00:29.377
KEY protects relationships to parent rows One
beginner detail

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:35.570
is especially important CHECK does not automatically
make a column required For

00:00:35.583 --> 00:00:39.597
example a check that quantity is greater than zero
only evaluates the

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:44.310
quantity when a value is present If quantity must
always be present

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.254
combine the check with NOT NULL The database should
enforce important rules

00:00:50.281 --> 00:00:54.557
whenever possible instead of relying only on
application code or user memory
